+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+`ToolRegistry.execute` validates a tool call against the resolved definition's `inputSchema` before invoking its executor. A rejected call is returned as a `ToolResponse`, while an accepted call reaches the executor with its input unchanged ([validated by: returns a required-field rejection without invoking the executor, then preserves valid extra input](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L11)).
+
+A wrong-typed field is rejected with a message that identifies the field and expected type without exposing the offending value ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed field with its path and expected type, without exposing the value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L39)).
+
+A function-valued tool definition is resolved and validated against its current schema on each call, rather than a stale schema ([validated by: validates a function-valued definition against the schema resolved for that call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L61)).
+
+A static tool schema is compiled when the tool is registered, so an uncompilable schema fails registration and identifies its tool ([validated by: throws with the tool name when a static schema cannot be compiled at registration](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L87)).
+
+A static schema is not recompiled on each execution ([validated by: compiles a static schema once across repeated executions](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L95)).
